Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: report tx airtime and enable airtime fairness

The airtime fairness scheduler in mac80211 charges a per station deficit
from the airtime the driver registers, and has no estimator fallback: with
no registered airtime the deficit never moves, which is why
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AIRTIME_FAIRNESS must not be set without the
reporting. Without it airtime_weight is refused with -EOPNOTSUPP and a
slow station can take two thirds of the medium from a fast one.

The ppdu stats path already extracts the frame exchange duration the
hardware reports for a completed PPDU and stores it in arsta->tx_duration
for the station dump. Register the same value with mac80211 and advertise
airtime fairness.

This is a backport of patch 4/9 of the series

  [PATCH ath-next v3 0/9] wifi: ath11k: airtime queue limits, fairness and
  a driver TXQ scheduler

posted to linux-wireless by Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
(message-id 20260824142350.1757379-1-julius@bairaktaris.de). The series is
not merged upstream yet and the original diffs were not reachable from the
build host, so the change was reimplemented against backports 6.18.26 from
the series description. It therefore carries no upstream Signed-off-by and
may differ from the patch that eventually lands.

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
index 4a45335..4c6aa82 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_rx.c
@@ -1487,6 +1487,13 @@ ath11k_update_per_peer_tx_stats(struct ath11k *ar,
 	arsta->tx_duration += tx_duration;
 	memcpy(&arsta->last_txrate, &arsta->txrate, sizeof(struct rate_info));
 
+	/* Feed the hardware's own view of the transmit airtime to the airtime
+	 * fairness scheduler. Without this the per station deficit is never
+	 * charged and NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AIRTIME_FAIRNESS cannot be set.
+	 */
+	if (tx_duration && tid < HTT_PPDU_STATS_NON_QOS_TID)
+		ieee80211_sta_register_airtime(sta, tid, tx_duration, 0);
+
 	/* PPDU stats reported for mgmt packet doesn't have valid tx bytes.
 	 * So skip peer stats update for mgmt packets.
 	 */
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index 88b3478..ae37f0e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -10439,6 +10439,14 @@ static int __ath11k_mac_register(struct ath11k *ar)
 	 * no AQM and no flow separation.
 	 */
 	wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy, NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL);
+
+	/* The transmit airtime the deficit is charged with is reported from
+	 * the ppdu stats path, and the receive airtime from the monitor
+	 * status ring; there is no estimator fallback, so the feature bit
+	 * must not be set without that reporting.
+	 */
+	wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy,
+			      NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AIRTIME_FAIRNESS);
 	if (test_bit(WMI_TLV_SERVICE_BSS_COLOR_OFFLOAD,
 		     ar->ab->wmi_ab.svc_map)) {
 		wiphy_ext_feature_set(ar->hw->wiphy,
